## OptionalDeps: Daseeki-Core, Daseeki-Bags, ItemRack, OPie
## Version: 1.3.3

# DaseekiArmoryScanDB is RETIRED as of 1.3.1 and is still declared on purpose.
# Nothing in normal play reads, writes or creates it — the item database is shipped
# in catalog.lua — but a declaration is dropped a couple of releases AFTER its last
# writer, never in the same build, so that a downgrade cannot meet an undeclared
# global and whatever an older build left on disk stays readable. Remove after 1.3.3.

core.lua
catalog.lua
pvpItems.lua
restrictions.lua
itemScan.lua
iconData.lua
sets.lua
equip.lua
keybind.lua
flyout.lua
setFlyout.lua
# chatdock.lua: the set swapper's "Chat" placement — a vertical column of set
# icons anchored outside Daseeki-Chat's chassis, sized so ten fit the panel.
# Loads with the other swapper surfaces and BEFORE widget.lua, which asks it
# which mode the swapper is effectively running in.
#
# NO OptionalDeps LINE IS NEEDED FOR IT, on purpose. Daseeki-Chat publishes its
# attach surface at FILE-LOAD time, and every enabled addon's files execute
# before PLAYER_LOGIN — which is when Addon:InitChatDock subscribes. So the
# surface is there in either load order, and the subscription answers
# immediately with whatever is true at that moment. Declaring a load order would
# buy nothing and would imply a dependency that does not exist: with
# Daseeki-Chat absent this file creates no frame at all and the swapper runs in
# its shipped default mode.
chatdock.lua
opie.lua
slotpopout.lua
paperdoll.lua
statmath.lua
stats.lua
trinkets.lua
borders.lua
tooltip.lua
iconPicker.lua
goalPicker.lua
widget.lua
options.lua
slash.lua
